# Resolution records cite source paths that contain `__tests__`. Prettier's Markdown
# printer rewrites `__x__` emphasis to `**x**`, which silently corrupts those paths and
# makes `node scripts/verify-resolutions.mjs --batch SYNC-<n>` fail its range check.
# Keep the records out of formatting so their paths stay literal.
docs/upstream-sync/resolutions/

# Sealed experiment artefacts. The fixture generators emit two-space JSON and their
# `--check` compares byte-for-byte. On 2026-11-16 a lint-staged prettier pass rewrote
# plan.json, answer-key.json and _label-map.json from two spaces to tabs (values
# unchanged), which broke `--check` and altered the bytes of an answer key that was
# sealed before the run. Formatting must never touch these again.
#
# The rule covers the whole frames directory, not one round: E20 and E20b
# (`e20/`, `e20b/`) are generated the same way, and a path-specific rule would
# silently leave their sealed answer keys formattable.
test-fixtures/frames/

# Upstream-identical formatting is a gate, not a preference. `gate:sync` step 2
# (verify-upstream-code-index-alignment) requires the `AvailableEmbedders` union to
# match `upstream/main` byte-for-byte, i.e. on one line; prettier 3.8.4 re-expands
# it into a multi-line union. The pre-commit hook runs `prettier --write` over
# `*.{ts,tsx,…}`, so without this rule the next routine edit to the file silently
# re-breaks the alignment gate (SYNC-23 CP2 F-03).
src/services/code-index/interfaces/embedder.ts
